diagnosis_text:
A full inspection of all five routers and both hosts in the dc_clos_bgp topology finds no fault. End-to-end reachability between pc_0_0 (10.0.0.2) and pc_0_1 (10.0.1.2) is confirmed: the ping completed with 0 % packet loss and a traceroute traversed the expected four-hop path (pc_0_0 → leaf_router_0_0 → spine_router_0_0 → leaf_router_0_1 → pc_0_1) with replies at every hop. All BGP sessions across the fabric are in Established state — both leaf routers peer successfully with both spine routers, and both spine routers peer with super_spine_router_0. The FIB on every device contains correct BGP-learned routes: 10.0.0.0/24 and 10.0.1.0/24 are present and active. Each leaf additionally holds a valid backup BGP path via spine_router_0_1, so redundancy is intact. Interface error and drop counters are zero on every link. The hosts carry no iptables rules and are correctly pointed to their respective leaf gateways (10.0.0.1 and 10.0.1.1). The reported symptom — inability to reach pc_0_1 from pc_0_0 — is not reproducible and is not supported by any evidence in the live lab. The ticket appears to describe a transient condition that had already resolved before this investigation began, or the perception of a fault that does not correspond to an actual network failure. No corrective action is required; the network is operating as designed.
=== END ===